cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cellscribe in your research, please cite it as below, together with the methods listed in the report's 'How to cite' section."
type: software
title: "Cellscribe: automated first-pass quality control, clustering and annotation reports for single-cell and spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  Cellscribe generates self-contained HTML reports from single-cell RNA-seq and
  spatial transcriptomics count matrices (10x Genomics, AnnData, CSV, Visium,
  Xenium). It performs MAD-based quality control, doublet detection, Leiden
  clustering with automatic resolution selection, a per-cluster QC breakdown that
  exposes technical artefacts, marker-based cell-type candidate scoring against a
  curated reference, and spatial statistics, and records every parameter for
  reproducibility.
authors:
